---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/main-layout.astro'
---

<MainLayout
  title="Before You Join | Silent Book Club Stourbridge"
  description="What to expect before joining the SBC Stourbridge WhatsApp Community — how groups work, At Home sessions, in-person meets, privacy and our community guidelines."
>

  <section
    class="w-full bg-primary-slate h-[35vh] lg:h-[50vh] flex justify-center items-end"
    aria-labelledby="page-title"
  >
    <div class="py-[30px] lg:py-[41px] px-6 sm:px-12 lg:px-16 flex flex-col justify-center items-center bg-white gap-2.5">
      <h1 id="page-title" class="text-[30px] leading-[1.25] lg:text-[50px] lg:leading-[1.24] font-dm text-primary-slate text-center">
        Before You Join the SBC Stourbridge WhatsApp Community
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="w-full page-section-y page-section-x mx-auto bg-white"
    aria-labelledby="page-title"
  >
    <div class="page-container w-full max-w-[65ch] lg:max-w-[900px] flex flex-col gap-10 text-base md:text-[18px] font-mulish text-text-gray leading-[1.5]">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <p>Welcome to Silent Book Club Stourbridge!</p>
        <p>
          Our WhatsApp Community is where members can keep in touch between meets, share what they're reading, take part in our virtual At Home sessions and find out about upcoming events.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before requesting access, please take a moment to read through the information below so you know what to expect.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-it-works-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="how-it-works-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          📚 How the WhatsApp Community Works
        </h2>
        <p>
          SBC Stourbridge is designed to be a friendly, welcoming and low-pressure community.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can participate as much or as little as you like. You don't need to attend every meet, join every conversation or be active in the WhatsApp groups to be considered part of the community.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no expectation that members will respond to messages, explain why they can't attend a meet or take part in conversations.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Participation is always optional.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Our WhatsApp Community contains different groups and channels for different purposes. Not every group is necessarily available to every member, and access may depend on the purpose of the group or activity.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="general-group-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="general-group-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          💬 The General Group
        </h2>
        <p>The General group is our main community chat.</p>
        <p>It's a place to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-1">
          <li>Chat about books and reading.</li>
          <li>Share recommendations.</li>
          <li>Talk about upcoming SBC Stourbridge activities.</li>
          <li>Get to know other members.</li>
          <li>Share relevant bookish news, events and discussions.</li>
          <li>Have the occasional conversation about things beyond books.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Please remember that this is a shared group. Not everyone will want to participate in every conversation, and members may have different levels of activity.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Participate as much or as little as you'd like, while being mindful of the space you're sharing with everyone else.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Be particularly mindful of the volume and frequency of messages you send in larger groups. There's plenty of room for conversation, but try to avoid sending a volume of messages that overwhelms conversations or generates excessive notifications for other members.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="at-home-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="at-home-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          🏠 At Home
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our At Home meets are virtual reading sessions that take place through WhatsApp.
        </p>
        <p>
          On an At Home evening, members read wherever they happen to be and can share what they're reading in the At Home group.
        </p>
        <p>
          The At Home group is generally kept quiet between sessions so that members aren't receiving notifications throughout the week. The group is opened for the relevant meet and then locked again afterwards.
        </p>
        <p>
          You don't need to attend an in-person meet to take part in At Home, and you don't need to take part in At Home to attend our in-person meets.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="in-person-meets-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="in-person-meets-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          📍 In-Person Meets
        </h2>
        <p>
          SBC Stourbridge also holds regular in-person Silent Book Club meets at venues around Stourbridge and the surrounding area.
        </p>
        <p>Our meets usually consist of:</p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Social time → Quiet reading time → Social time</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          The quiet reading period is the heart of Silent Book Club. Everyone brings whatever book they are currently reading and reads alongside the group.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no assigned book and no requirement to discuss what you're reading.
        </p>
        <p>
          Socialising before and after the reading period is encouraged, but it is always optional.
        </p>
        <h3
          id="booking-a-meet-heading"
          class="text-[22px] md:text-[28px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] text-primary-slate font-bold mt-2"
        >
          Booking a meet
        </h3>
        <p>
          Places at our in-person meets are managed through Eventbrite.
        </p>
        <p>
          Joining the WhatsApp Community <strong class="text-primary-slate">does not automatically book you onto a meet</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you would like to attend an in-person meet, please follow the Eventbrite link provided on our website or social media and book a place where required.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some venues have limited capacity, so a place at a meet should always be booked in advance where an RSVP is required.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="other-groups-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="other-groups-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          👥 Other Groups and Channels
        </h2>
        <p>
          SBC Stourbridge has additional groups and channels for particular activities, events and types of conversation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">You don't need to join every group, and joining the WhatsApp Community does not automatically give you access to every group.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Some groups may be open to all members, while others may be restricted, invitation-only or created for a specific purpose.
        </p>
        <p>
          Admins may approve or decline requests to join individual groups. This helps us keep each space manageable and ensures that groups remain useful for their intended purpose.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="getting-to-know-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="getting-to-know-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          🤝 Getting to Know Other Members
        </h2>
        <p>
          One of the lovely things about Silent Book Club is that members can meet other people who enjoy reading.
        </p>
        <p>
          Members are welcome to chat with one another and, where both people are comfortable, communicate privately.
        </p>
        <p>
          However, please remember that <strong class="text-primary-slate">being a member of SBC Stourbridge does not automatically give you permission to contact another member privately or request their personal contact details.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          If someone doesn't respond to a message, doesn't wish to continue a conversation, or asks you not to contact them privately, please respect their decision.
        </p>
        <p>Nobody should feel pressured to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 flex flex-col gap-1">
          <li>Give out their telephone number or other personal details.</li>
          <li>Attend a meet.</li>
          <li>Stay at a meet.</li>
          <li>Join a conversation.</li>
          <li>Respond to a message.</li>
          <li>Meet another member privately.</li>
          <li>Explain why they have chosen not to participate.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-safety-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="privacy-safety-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          🔒 Your Privacy and Safety
        </h2>
        <p>
          Please use your own judgement when sharing personal information with other members.
        </p>
        <p>
          You are never required to provide your telephone number, address, workplace, social media details or other personal information to participate in SBC Stourbridge.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you choose to meet another member privately or outside an official SBC Stourbridge activity, please make your own arrangements to stay safe and let someone you trust know where you are going and who you are meeting.
        </p>
        <p>
          Please also respect the privacy of other members. Do not share their personal information, photographs, screenshots or private conversations outside the community without their permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="leave-whenever-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="leave-whenever-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          👋 You Can Leave Whenever You Like
        </h2>
        <p>
          You are always welcome to leave any SBC Stourbridge WhatsApp group if you no longer wish to participate in it.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is <strong class="text-primary-slate">no obligation to remain in a group</strong>, and leaving one group does not mean you have to leave the wider SBC Stourbridge community.
        </p>
        <p>
          Likewise, please respect the decision of anyone who chooses to leave a group. There is no need to ask them to justify their decision or pressure them to return.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="guidelines-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="guidelines-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          📖 Our Community Guidelines
        </h2>
        <p>
          We have a set of Community Guidelines covering personal safety, privacy, WhatsApp etiquette, in-person meet etiquette, respecting other members and how our admins manage the community.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Please read the full guidelines before joining the WhatsApp Community.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/communityguidelines" class="text-primary-slate hover:underline focus-ring rounded-sm">
            Read the SBC Stourbridge Community Guidelines
          </a>
        </p>
        <p>
          They aren't intended to stop people having fun or making friends. They're there to help us maintain the relaxed, welcoming and low-pressure atmosphere that makes SBC Stourbridge what it is.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="admins-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="admins-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          🛡️ Admins
        </h2>
        <p>
          SBC Stourbridge is run by volunteer admins who give their time alongside their own personal and work commitments.
        </p>
        <p>
          Admins monitor the WhatsApp groups and may step in if a conversation or behaviour becomes disruptive, inappropriate or causes concern.
        </p>
        <p>
          If another member makes you uncomfortable, pressures you for personal information, repeatedly contacts you when you don't wish to engage, or behaves in a way that affects your ability to participate comfortably, <strong class="text-primary-slate">please speak to an admin rather than feeling that you have to deal with it yourself.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          Admins may restrict or remove access to individual groups, events or the wider community where necessary to protect the safety, wellbeing and enjoyment of members.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="short-version-heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
        <h2
          id="short-version-heading"
          class="text-[30px] font-nunito tracking-wide leading-[1.25] md:text-[40px] text-primary-slate font-bold"
        >
          ❤️ The Short Version
        </h2>
        <p>If you remember nothing else, remember these:</p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Read what you like.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Come to as many or as few meets as you want.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Participate as much or as little as you'd like — while being mindful of the space you're sharing with everyone else.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">You never have to give anyone your personal details.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Respect other people's boundaries and choices.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">You can leave a group whenever you want.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-primary-slate">Participation is always optional.</strong>
        </p>
        <p>
          And most importantly, <strong class="text-primary-slate">have fun and enjoy being part of the SBC Stourbridge community!</strong>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
